# S20_tape (D-SESSIONS, 2026-11-13): the cassette round trip AT THE PROMPT -- a program
# CSAVEd, then CLOADed back and LISTed / RUN; the same through SAVE"CAS:" (ASCII) and LOAD;
# a block of RAM through BSAVE"CAS:" and BLOAD"CAS:". The recorder is openMSX's: a blank
# tape to record on, then `cassetteplayer play` + `rewind` to read back what this machine
# wrote. The VG-8020 against zerobas (the nodisk target). The waits after each save are
# the APPARATUS's: the runner's idle test (CURLIN still, the key buffer empty) also holds
# during a tape write, so without them the recorder was switched to play before BSAVE's
# data block was on the tape (sessions_S20_tape2.out: the VG-8020 never found BLK, zerobas
# Device I/O error). SAVE "CAS:" waits longest: 6 s after it the VG-8020 was still writing
# where zerobas showed Ok (sessions_S20_tape3.out, snapshot 10) -- a timing difference, filed
# under D-SESSIONS, not a result.
{TCL cassetteplayer new {TMP}_t.wav}
NEW
10 PRINT "TAPE SESSION"
20 FOR I=1 TO 3:PRINT I*11:NEXT
CSAVE "PROG"
{WAIT 6}
SAVE "CAS:ASC"
{WAIT 14}
FOR I=0 TO 15:POKE &HD000+I,I*7:NEXT
BSAVE "CAS:BLK",&HD000,&HD00F
{WAIT 10}
{TCL cassetteplayer play}
{TCL cassetteplayer rewind}
NEW
CLOAD "PROG"
LIST
RUN
NEW
LOAD "CAS:ASC"
LIST
FOR I=0 TO 15:POKE &HD000+I,0:NEXT
BLOAD "CAS:BLK"
S=0:FOR I=0 TO 15:S=S+PEEK(&HD000+I)*(I+1):NEXT:PRINT S
